JIT write-protect toggles only when the state changes (M9 track,
docs/tracks/m9-tcg-aarch64.md). On macOS the code buffer is MAP_JIT and each
thread flips it between writable and executable with
pthread_jit_write_protect_np(); QEMU calls the executable side before every TB
it runs from the main loop (cpu_tb_exec) and the writable side around every
jump patch, translation and invalidation, without remembering the state. A
guest that returns to the main loop often (Super PI: x87 helpers that end their
TB) spent 12 % of its vCPU thread in that call on an M1. A per-thread state
skips the redundant calls; it starts as unknown, so a thread's first request in
either direction is made for real (the main thread is in execute mode when
tcg_prologue_init asks for write; a skipped call there faults and spins).

diff --git a/include/qemu/osdep.h b/include/qemu/osdep.h
index 1ec5b42230..f8577bbefa 100644
--- a/include/qemu/osdep.h
+++ b/include/qemu/osdep.h
@@ -845,14 +845,31 @@ size_t qemu_get_host_physmem(void);
  * for the current thread.
  */
 #ifdef __APPLE__
+/*
+ * The state is tracked per thread so that the switch is only made when
+ * it changes: cpu_tb_exec() asks for execute before every TB it runs from
+ * the main loop, and a guest that returns to the main loop often (x87
+ * helpers that end their TB, unchained exits) spent 12 % of its vCPU time
+ * in pthread_jit_write_protect_np() on an M1 (M9 track profile, Super PI).
+ * A thread's real state is unknown until it asked once (-1): the first
+ * request in either direction makes the call.
+ */
+extern __thread int qemu_thread_jit_state;   /* -1 unknown, 0 execute, 1 write */
+
 static inline void qemu_thread_jit_execute(void)
 {
-    pthread_jit_write_protect_np(true);
+    if (qemu_thread_jit_state != 0) {
+        pthread_jit_write_protect_np(true);
+        qemu_thread_jit_state = 0;
+    }
 }
 
 static inline void qemu_thread_jit_write(void)
 {
-    pthread_jit_write_protect_np(false);
+    if (qemu_thread_jit_state != 1) {
+        pthread_jit_write_protect_np(false);
+        qemu_thread_jit_state = 1;
+    }
 }
 #else
 static inline void qemu_thread_jit_write(void) {}
